 "constraints": [],
 "stem": "Using synthetic division, find the remainder when $A = {=p}x^2 {=qs}x {=rs}$ is divided by $B = x - {=a}$. Answer only the remainder.",
 "answer": "rem",
 "solution": [
  "Coefficients of $A$: {=p}, {=q}, {=r}. The divisor is $x - {=a}$, so write {=a} on the left.",
  "Bring down {=p}. Multiply: ${=p}\\times{=a}={=m1}$, and add: ${=q}+({=m1})={=s1}$.",
  "Multiply: ${=s1}\\times{=a}={=m2}$, and add: ${=r}+({=m2})={=rem}$.",
  "Bottom row: {=p}, {=s1}, remainder {=rem}. The quotient is ${=p}x + ({=s1})$ and the remainder is {=rem}."
 ],
